                  <provenance type="#e"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_465">Rievaulx, Yorkshire.
                        Cistercian abbey of St Mary the Virgin</orgName><p>(fol. 1r) 'Liber sancte
                        Marie Rievale'.</p><p>On fol. ir is the copy of a bond for £40 between Abbot
                        William, Sir William Pickering of Oswaldkirk (d. 1542, who acquired
                        considerable ex-monastic property), William Priestman, yeoman of
                        Newtongrange (perhaps the tenant of Rievaulx of that name reported at the
                        time of the suppression), and William Walton, yeoman of Newtongrange.
                        William was abbot 1513–28.</p><p>(Medieval binding.)</p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">'Richardum Gyllyne monachum Rievallys', i.e.
                     Richard Hall, alias Gilling, monk of Rievaulx at surrender in 1538, later vicar
                     of Laytham (Yorks); will dated 1 March 1565.</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">'Ricardus 1569' (front
                     pastedown).</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners"> At foot of fol. ir is the ex libris of John
                     Dodsworth of Thornton Wetlass, probably the John Thornton born in 1569 who made
                     his will in January 1640.</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Christie's sale 30 May 1984, lot
                     207.</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners"> </provenance>
               </history>
